From 01a2013e26bf1124fee1dc6cbd0da913fd96325b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Refactor Bot <refactor@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 06:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] refactor(content): introduce a single, locale-aware
 content layer

Content previously lived in four inconsistent places (next-intl messages,
English-only TS data modules, in-component constants, and the deleted JSON
CMS). This adds one CMS-agnostic content API that the app reads through:

- lib/content/types.ts    domain models + Localized<T> + resolve() fallback
- lib/content/data/*      localized source data (services incl. fa; demo
                          testimonials/projects moved out of components)
- lib/content/adapters/local.ts   resolves data for the active locale
- lib/content/provider.ts selects the backend (env-switchable)
- lib/content/index.ts    public API: getServices/getTestimonials/
                          getFeaturedProjects/getIndustries/getIndustry

Wiring:
- Home, Services, Industries (now a Server Component) and the industry detail
  page fetch content and pass it down; presentational components take props.
- ServicesTeaserGrid/TestimonialsGrid/ServicesListing/FeaturedProjectsCarousel
  no longer import data directly; carousel types come from lib/content.
- Deleted components/home/{services,testimonials}-data.ts.

Also fixes a React 19 set-state-in-effect lint error in CookieConsentBanner
(now uses useSyncExternalStore). The getters are async so the Payload adapter
(next) is a drop-in behind ContentSource.
